Subject: [DIAGNOSTIC ONLY] virtio_balloon: retain one disposable reporting page

Linux 7.2.2; apply after the existing Silo live and x86_64 patches.
Default-off, built-in x86_64 diagnostic, not production allocator reacquisition
or destructive-reclaim qualification. No ordinary page_reporting supplier is
registered in this build. The single page stays allocated through the exact
used completion, guest C reuse, capture, and fresh-restore verification.

diff --git a/drivers/virtio/Kconfig b/drivers/virtio/Kconfig
--- a/drivers/virtio/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/virtio/Kconfig
@@ -132,6 +132,19 @@
 
 	 If unsure, say M.
 
+config VIRTIO_BALLOON_SILO_RECLAIM_DIAG
+	bool "Silo owned disposable page reporting diagnostic"
+	depends on VIRTIO_BALLOON=y && X86_64 && SYSFS
+	default n
+	help
+	  Reserve the balloon reporting queue exclusively for a root-only,
+	  one-page retained-allocation diagnostic via the device's silo_reclaim
+	  sysfs attribute. Ordinary page_reporting is not registered.
+
+	  This is not production allocator reacquisition or destructive reclaim
+	  qualification. Select only in a separately identified diagnostic image.
+	  If unsure, say N.
+
